From 139976220df0c7553ea3529c18be03900f451c71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:26:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 132/132] fs: remember where a path resolved, so a build asks
 the filesystem once per path

Container::resolve looked every path up again on each read: an exact check in every mountpoint, then, for a
path in none of them, the same mountpoints again ignoring case, which lists directories. A build asks for the
same paths many times: one launch of 3042492564 (strace, warm) opened common.h 177 times and common_blending.h 99,
and listed the zcompat shader folder 226 times, the scene folder 355 and materials 128, for paths that never
match exactly (5042 opens, 5078 stats, 1451 directory reads in all).

resolve now keeps each answer (the adapter and the path to open on it, or "in no mountpoint"), keyed by the path
as asked, for as long as the mountpoints and the VFS stay as they were: a mount, or a VFS add (VirtualAdapter's
new generation counter), drops them all. A remembered hit still reopens the file, so a read sees the file as it
is now. While the health report is on nothing is remembered: it records each lookup's own outcome (a case-only
match is reported once per lookup). The cache has its own lock: lookups may come from other threads.

Measured (same player, warm medians of 8, with the upload context patch on both sides): 3042492564's file
lookups during the build 72 -> 49 ms and first frame 596 -> 567 ms; 3163060610 32 -> 24 and 501 -> 479; the
other scenes within noise. Same pictures as without it.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/TODO.md (scene wallpapers load faster)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
